        <headline>Coastal Flood Advisory issued September 25 at 5:27AM EDT until September 27 at 6:00PM EDT by NWS Upton NY</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...One to two feet of inundation above ground level
expected in vulnerable areas near the waterfront and shoreline.

* WHERE...Hudson, Eastern Essex and Eastern Union Counties.

* WHEN...From 6 PM this evening to 6 PM EDT Sunday.

* IMPACTS...Minor to locally flooding in the more vulnerable
locations near the waterfront and shoreline. Some roads and low
lying properties including parking lots, parks, lawns, and homes
and businesses with basements near the waterfront will
experience minor flooding.
</description>
        <instruction>If travel is required, allow extra time as some roads may be
closed. Do not drive around barricades or through water of
unknown depth. Take the necessary actions to protect flood-prone
property.</instruction>
